#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:126
msgid "Search modifiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:128
msgid ""
"You can apply search modifiers to any search to reduce the number of "
"results returned. Select a search modifier to add it to the Search field."
" Supported modifiers are described below. Your search results include "
"messages from all of your teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:131
msgid "``from:`` and ``in:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:133
msgid "Use ``from:`` to find messages or files from specific users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:135
msgid ""
"For example, searching ``from:john.smith`` only returns content from your"
" direct message history with John Smith."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:136
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.10, you can use ``from:`` in cross-team searches to "
"find messages from specific users across all teams you're a member of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:138
msgid ""
"Use ``in:`` to find messages or files posted in specific public channels,"
" private channels, direct messages, or group messages. You can specify "
"channels by display name or channel ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:140
msgid ""
"For example, searching ``Mattermost in:town-square`` only returns results"
" in the Town Square public channel that contains the term ``Mattermost``,"
" while searching ``Mattermost in:john.doe`` only returns results that "
"contains the term ``Mattermost`` in your direct message history with John"
" Smith."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:143
msgid "``before:``, ``after:``, and ``on:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:145
msgid "Use ``before:`` to find messages or files posted before a specified date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:147
msgid ""
"For example, searching ``website before: 2018-09-01`` returns messages or"
" files containing the term ``website`` posted prior to September 1, 2018."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:149
msgid "Use ``after:`` to find messages or files posted after a specified date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:151
msgid ""
"For example, searching ``website after: 2018-08-01`` returns messages or "
"files containing the term ``website`` posted after August 1, 2018."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:153
msgid ""
"Use both ``before:`` and ``after:`` together to search in a specified "
"date range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:155
msgid ""
"For example, searching ``website before: 2018-09-01 after: 2018-08-01`` "
"returns all messages or files containing the term ``website`` posted "
"between August 1, 2018 and September 1, 2018."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:157
msgid ""
"Use ``on:`` to find messages or files posted on a specific date. Use the "
"date picker to select a date, or type it in YYYY-MM-DD format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:159
msgid ""
"For example, searching ``website on: 2018-09-01`` returns messages or "
"files containing the term ``website`` posted on September 1, 2018."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:161
msgid "Select the on modifier to specify messages or files for a specific a date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:166
msgid "Exclusions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:168
msgid ""
"Use the hyphen ``-`` symbol to exclude terms from your search results. "
"For example, searching ``test -release`` only returns results that "
"include the term ``test`` and exclude the term ``release``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:170
msgid ""
"This exclusion modifier can be used in combination with other modifiers "
"to further refine search results. For example, searching ``test -release "
"-in:release-discussion -from:eric`` returns all results with the term "
"``test``, excludes posts with the term ``release``, excludes posts made "
"in the ``release-discussion`` channel, and excludes messages sent in "
"direct messages by ``eric``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:173
msgid "Quotation marks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:175
msgid ""
"Use quotation marks ``\" \"`` to return search results for exact terms. "
"For example, searching ``\"Mattermost website\"`` returns messages "
"containing the exact phrase ``Mattermost website``, but doesn't return "
"results containing ``Mattermost`` and ``website`` as separate terms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:178
msgid "Wildcards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:180
msgid ""
"Use the asterisk ``*`` symbol at the end of the word to perform a "
"wildcard search. The wildcard search returns all words that begin with "
"the specified letters. The wildcard in search cannot be used at the "
"beginning or in the middle of a word. For example, searching ``rea*`` "
"returns messages or files containing words like ``reach``, ``reason``, "
"``reality``, ``real``, and other words starting with ``rea``. However, "
"searches like ``*each`` and ``re*ch`` are invalid wildcard searches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:183
msgid "Hashtags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:185
msgid ""
"Hashtags are searchable labels for messages. Anyone can create a hashtag "
"in a message by using the pound sign ``#`` followed by alphanumeric or "
"other unicode characters. Hashtag examples include: ``#bug``, "
"``#marketing``, ``#user_testing``, ``#per.iod``, ``#check-in``, ``#마케팅``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:187
msgid "Valid hashtags:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:189
msgid "Don't start with a number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:190
msgid "Are at least three characters long, excluding the ``#``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:191
msgid "Are made up of alphanumeric or other unicode characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:192
msgid "May contain dots, dashes, or underscores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:194
msgid ""
"To search for messages containing hashtags, select a hashtag in an "
"existing post, or type the hashtag (including the pound ``#`` symbol) "
"into the search bar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:198
msgid ""
"Hashtags don't link to channels. If you have a channel named “Marketing”,"
" selecting a ``#marketing`` hashtag does not take you to the Marketing "
"channel. To link to public channels, use the tilde ``~`` symbol followed "
"by the channel name. For example ``~marketing``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:201
msgid "Search public channels you haven't joined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/ent-plus.rst:9
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Enterprise and Enterprise Advanced plans"
" <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:206
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v11.6, when your system admin :ref:`enables searching "
"public channels without membership <administration-guide/configure"
"/environment-configuration-settings:allow searching public channels "
"without membership>`, search results can include messages from public "
"channels you haven't joined. Results are scoped to teams you belong to, "
"so you'll only see messages from public channels in your teams. This "
"setting doesn't affect private channels — you can only search private "
"channels you're a member of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:209
msgid "Notes about performing Mattermost searches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:211
msgid ""
"Multiple-word searches return results that contain *all* of your search "
"criteria."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:212
msgid ""
"Search modifiers can help narrow down searches. See the `search modifiers"
" <#search-modifiers>`__ section for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:213
msgid ""
"You can search Archived channels as long as you're a member of that "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:215
msgid ""
"If you're unable to see messages or files in archived channels in your "
"search results, ask your system admin if **Allow users to view archived "
"channels** has been disabled via **System Console > Site Configuration > "
"Users and Teams**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:216
msgid ""
"To remove archived channels from your search results, you can leave the "
"Archived channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:217
msgid ""
"Like many search engines, common words such as ``the``, ``which``, and "
"``are`` (known as \"stop words\"), as well as two-letter and one-letter "
"search terms, are not shown in search results because they typically "
"return too many results. See the `Technical notes about searching "
"<#technical-notes-about-searching>`__ section below for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:218
msgid "IP addresses (e.g. ``10.100.200.101``) don't return results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:221
msgid "Technical notes about searching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:223
msgid ""
"By default, Mattermost uses full text search support included in "
"PostgreSQL. Select the **product menu** |product-list| then select "
"**About Mattermost** to see which database you’re using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:100
msgid ""
"Navigate between Channels, collaborative playbooks, and boards using the "
"product menu icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:225
msgid ""
"Stop words are filtered out of search results. See `PostgreSQL "
"<https://www.postgresql.org/docs/10/textsearch-dictionaries.html"
"#TEXTSEARCH-STOPWORDS>`__ database documentation for a full list of "
"applicable stop words."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:226
msgid "URLs don’t return results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:227
msgid ""
"Hashtags or recent mentions of usernames containing a dash don't return "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/search-for-messages.rst:228
